    <name>🌫️ LIVE FOG RISK/ACTIVE FOG</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Time fetched:</b> Oct 6, 2026 6:12AM EDT</p><h2>LIVE FOG RISK/ACTIVE FOG</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/fog/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>Fog-risk index 0-100 (DERIVED from HRRR analysis, fixed absolute scale): <b>LOWEST 0</b> green low risk &rarr; yellow elevated &rarr; orange high &rarr; red very high &rarr; <b>ACTIVE FOG 85+</b> red-violet into deep purple dense active fog (visibility-confirmed) to <b>HIGHEST+ 100</b>. Same index always shows the same color. Thermodynamic risk with a visibility confirmation gate — not a copy of the visibility layer.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/NCEP HRRR 3 km analysis, hourly cycles: TMP+DPT+RH (2 m) + UGRD/VGRD (10 m) + VIS surface (derived fog-risk index with active-fog visibility gate)).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
